// GFX-1's part 6, step 4: a golden for each feature GFX-1 built that draws something of its own and had none under its
// name (kyoten's rendering.md § Decided, step 4's second asking, question 2: FEATURES.md's test is "the feature's
// golden-image test, with a golden per method"). Each is a small scene in which the feature changes pixels, drawn on the
// leg's software GPU and compared byte for byte with `tests/goldens/<test>/<gpu>.png`, named as FEATURES.md names the
// feature's test:
// - `scene-graph`: a turned, squashed group holding two boxes, one of them turned and holding a third, so each box sits
//   where its parents' transforms put it;
// - `camera-perspective`: three boxes going back from a wide camera into a 2:1 target, so each shrinks with its distance
//   and the frame keeps its aspect;
// - `depth-precision`: two broad slabs 5 km away whose faces are 5 cm apart, the nearer covering the farther where they
//   overlap, which reversed depth on a float target resolves and the standard convention cannot;
// - `geometry-primitives`: a box cut into 6 x 6 x 6 segments under a material that pulls each vertex towards a sphere,
//   so its faces round where a box with no segments would stay flat;
// - `render-target`: two boxes crossing in depth, drawn into a 50 x 30 target, its size and its depth the target's own;
// - `nodes`: a program's own node material: a world-space gradient mixed by height and shaded by a direction;
// - `nodes-override`: `MeshStandardMaterial` with its four slots set to nodes that vary over the surface, under a sun and
//   an ambient light;
// - `material-unlit`: `MeshBasicMaterial` beside `MeshStandardMaterial` of the same colour under a strong sun: the unlit
//   box one flat colour, the lit one shaded;
// - `light-units`: a box under a 100,000-lux sun and a 20,000-lux ambient light, seen at EV100 15, sunlight's exposure,
//   through the default tone mapping;
// - `exposure`: a box under three.js's default light, seen at a manual exposure 1.5 stops brighter, with no tone mapping.
//
// On every leg, each frame is held to being read back with something drawn, and the unlit box's faces and the slabs'
// overlap to their colours exactly; the goldens hold the rest. A step a tick, on the device the check opened.

import {
    std::collections::DynamicArray,
    std::math::Vec3, std::math::radians,
    std::time::Instant, std::time::monotonicNow,
    gpu::Device, gpu::Queue, gpu::DeviceErrors, gpu::GpuError,
    graphics::Color, graphics::Renderer, graphics::RenderTarget, graphics::Scene, graphics::Group, graphics::Mesh,
    graphics::PerspectiveCamera, graphics::ToneMapping, graphics::BoxGeometry, graphics::MeshBasicMaterial,
    graphics::MeshStandardMaterial, graphics::DirectionalLight, graphics::AmbientLight, graphics::Material,
    graphics::MaterialGpu, graphics::MaterialSettings, graphics::NodeBuilder, graphics::Euler, graphics::EulerOrder,
    graphics::PixelRead, graphics::PixelStatus, graphics::FloatNode, graphics::Vec3Node, graphics::Vec4Node,
    graphics::normalWorld, graphics::positionWorld, graphics::positionLocal, graphics::modelWorldMatrix,
    graphics::cameraViewProjectionMatrix, graphics::vec3, graphics::vec4, graphics::constant, graphics::normalize,
    graphics::mix, graphics::saturate, graphics::dot, graphics::ev100Sunlight, graphics::ev100For,
    gpuResolved, Verdicts, checkGolden, nearTo,
};
export { FeaturesRun };

comptime int64 SETTLE_MS = 10000;
comptime uint32 BACKDROP = 0x202830;
comptime int32 DONE = 999;

// A program's own material that rounds a box: each vertex pulled part of the way to the sphere through the box's
// corners, so a face with vertices inside it bulges and one with only its corners stays flat. Its colour is its face's
// normal, n / 2 + 1/2, unlit.
type resource Rounded implements Material {
    MaterialGpu cache;
    public ctor make() { this.cache = MaterialGpu.make(); }
    public fn ref MaterialGpu gpuMut() { return this.cache; }
    public const fn uint32 version() { return 0; }
    public const fn uint32 graphVersion() { return 0; }
    public const fn void settings(ref MaterialSettings into) { }
    public fn void shade(ref NodeBuilder builder) {
        Vec3Node pulled = normalize(v: positionLocal()) * 0.35 + positionLocal() * 0.6;
        Vec4Node world = modelWorldMatrix() * vec4(xyz: pulled, w: constant(value: 1.0));
        builder.vertexPosition(node: cameraViewProjectionMatrix() * world);
        Vec3Node half = vec3(x: constant(value: 0.5), y: constant(value: 0.5), z: constant(value: 0.5));
        builder.fragmentColor(node: vec4(xyz: normalWorld() * 0.5 + half, w: constant(value: 1.0)));
    }
}

// A program's own node material: warm at the bottom and cool at the top in world space, mixed by height, and shaded by
// how its normal faces a fixed direction.
type resource Gradient implements Material {
    MaterialGpu cache;
    public ctor make() { this.cache = MaterialGpu.make(); }
    public fn ref MaterialGpu gpuMut() { return this.cache; }
    public const fn uint32 version() { return 0; }
    public const fn uint32 graphVersion() { return 0; }
    public const fn void settings(ref MaterialSettings into) { }
    public fn void shade(ref NodeBuilder builder) {
        Vec3Node warm = vec3(x: constant(value: 0.9), y: constant(value: 0.3), z: constant(value: 0.1));
        Vec3Node cool = vec3(x: constant(value: 0.1), y: constant(value: 0.4), z: constant(value: 0.9));
        FloatNode height = positionWorld().y() + 0.5;
        FloatNode by = saturate(x: height);
        Vec3Node toward = normalize(v: vec3(x: constant(value: 1.0), y: constant(value: 2.0), z: constant(value: 3.0)));
        FloatNode facing = dot(a: normalWorld(), b: toward) * 0.5 + 0.5;
        Vec3Node shaded = mix(from: warm, to: cool, by: by) * facing;
        builder.fragmentColor(node: vec4(xyz: shaded, w: constant(value: 1.0)));
    }
}

type resource FeaturesRun {
    int32 stage = 0;
    Instant began = monotonicNow();
    string gpu;
    bool software;
    int32 declaredCount = 0;
    int32 matchedCount = 0;
    Verdicts found;
    Device device;
    Queue queue;
    Optional<Renderer> renderer = Optional::None;
    Optional<PixelRead> reading = Optional::None;
    DynamicArray<uint8> frame;
    string failed = "";
    uint32 wide = 0;
    uint32 high = 0;

    public ctor make(string gpu, bool software, Device device, Queue queue) {
        this.gpu = give gpu;
        this.software = software;
        this.found = Verdicts.make();
        this.device = give device;
        this.queue = give queue;
        this.frame = DynamicArray.empty();
    }

    public fn ref Verdicts verdicts() { return this.found; }
    public const fn int32 declared() { return this.declaredCount; }
    public const fn int32 matched() { return this.matchedCount; }

    unsafe fn void next(int32 to) { this.stage = to; this.began = monotonicNow(); }

    // The read's texels into `frame` once it answers; false while it is pending. A failed read leaves `failed` set.
    unsafe fn bool settled() {
        PixelStatus s = match (this.reading) {
            case Some(value: r): r.poll();
            case None: PixelStatus::Failed(error: GpuError::Refused(words: "no read was started"));
        };
        bool pending = match (s) { case Pending: true; case _: false; };
        if (pending && this.began.elapsed().asMillis() < SETTLE_MS) { return false; }
        this.frame = DynamicArray.empty();
        this.failed = "";
        match (give s) {
            case Ready(image: img): {
                borrow img.samples8() as px { for (isize i = 0; i < px.length(); i = i + 1) { this.frame.add(item: px[i]); } }
            }
            case Failed(error: e): { this.failed = "the read failed: " + e.message(); }
            case Pending: { this.failed = "the read was still pending after ${SETTLE_MS} ms"; }
        };
        this.reading = Optional::None;
        return true;
    }

    // The frame's texel (x, y), 0xRRGGBB, or 0xffffffff off the frame.
    unsafe fn uint32 texelAt(isize x, isize y) {
        isize w = cast<isize>(this.wide);
        isize h = cast<isize>(this.high);
        if (x < 0 || y < 0 || x >= w || y >= h) { return 0xffffffff; }
        isize at = (y * w + x) * 4;
        if (at + 2 >= this.frame.length()) { return 0xffffffff; }
        return (cast<uint32>(this.frame[at]) << 16) | (cast<uint32>(this.frame[at + 1]) << 8) | cast<uint32>(this.frame[at + 2]);
    }

    // `scene` through `cam` into a new `wide` x `high` target, and its read started.
    unsafe fn void draw(Shared<Scene> scene, Shared<PerspectiveCamera> cam, uint32 wide, uint32 high) {
        Shared<RenderTarget> t = new RenderTarget.make(width: wide, height: high);
        cam.targetMut() = Optional::Some(value: copy t);
        match (this.renderer) {
            case Some(value: r): {
                r.render(scene: scene, camera: cam);
                this.reading = Optional::Some(value: r.readRenderTargetPixels(target: copy t));
            }
            case None: { }
        };
        this.wide = wide;
        this.high = high;
    }

    // "" when the frame was read and something other than the backdrop was drawn.
    unsafe fn string drawn() {
        if (!this.failed.isEmpty()) { return copy this.failed; }
        for (isize y = 0; y < cast<isize>(this.high); y = y + 1) {
            for (isize x = 0; x < cast<isize>(this.wide); x = x + 1) {
                if (this.texelAt(x: x, y: y) != BACKDROP) { return ""; }
            }
        }
        return "every texel is the backdrop";
    }

    // The frame held to its golden on a leg that names a software GPU, and on every leg to being read with something drawn.
    unsafe fn void held(string test, string what) {
        this.found.add(name: test + ": " + what + ", read back with something drawn", why: this.drawn());
        if (this.gpu.isEmpty()) { return; }
        this.declaredCount = this.declaredCount + 1;
        string said = "the frame was not read: " + this.failed;
        if (this.failed.isEmpty()) {
            said = this.software ? checkGolden(test: test, gpu: this.gpu, width: cast<isize>(this.wide), height: cast<isize>(this.high), frame: this.frame)
                 : "the adapter is not the software GPU the leg names, so its frame is not compared";
        }
        if (said.isEmpty()) { this.matchedCount = this.matchedCount + 1; }
        this.found.add(name: "golden " + test + " on " + this.gpu, why: give said);
    }

    // A camera with no tone mapping at `eye`, looking at `at`.
    unsafe fn Shared<PerspectiveCamera> plainCamera(float32 fovDeg, float32 near, float32 far, Vec3 eye, Vec3 at) {
        Shared<PerspectiveCamera> cam = new PerspectiveCamera.make(fovRad: radians(deg: fovDeg), near: near, far: far);
        cam.toneMappingMut() = ToneMapping::None;
        cam.positionMut() = eye;
        cam.lookAt(target: at);
        return cam;
    }

    // An unlit box of `size` at `at`, `hex` its colour.
    unsafe fn Shared<Mesh> unlitBox(float32 size, Vec3 at, uint32 hex) {
        Shared<BoxGeometry> box = new BoxGeometry.make(width: size, height: size, depth: size);
        Shared<MeshBasicMaterial> look = new MeshBasicMaterial.make();
        look.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: hex);
        Shared<Mesh> m = new Mesh.make(geometry: box, material: look);
        m.positionMut() = at;
        return m;
    }

    // A box of `size` at `at` drawn with `look`.
    unsafe fn Shared<Mesh> boxWith(float32 size, Vec3 at, Shared<Material> look) {
        Shared<BoxGeometry> box = new BoxGeometry.make(width: size, height: size, depth: size);
        Shared<Mesh> m = new Mesh.make(geometry: box, material: look);
        m.positionMut() = at;
        return m;
    }

    public unsafe fn bool step() {
        if (this.stage == 0) {
            Renderer made = gpuResolved(device: copy this.device, queue: copy this.queue);
            made.clearColorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: BACKDROP);
            this.renderer = Optional::Some(value: give made);
            // scene-graph: a group turned 30 degrees about y and squashed, holding a red box and a green one turned 25
            // degrees about z, which holds a small blue box above it
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<Group> g = new Group.make();
            g.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 0.0, y: 30.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            g.scaleMut() = Vec3.of(x: 1.3, y: 0.7, z: 1.0);
            g.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.2, z: 0.0);
            Shared<Mesh> left = this.unlitBox(size: 0.6, at: Vec3.of(x: -0.9, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), hex: 0xd04030);
            Shared<Mesh> right = this.unlitBox(size: 0.6, at: Vec3.of(x: 0.9, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), hex: 0x40b050);
            right.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: 25.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            Shared<Mesh> top = this.unlitBox(size: 0.3, at: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.7, z: 0.0), hex: 0x4060e0);
            right.add(object: top);
            g.add(object: left);
            g.add(object: right);
            s.add(object: g);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 1.0, z: 4.0), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 1);
        } else if (this.stage == 1) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "scene-graph", what: "two boxes in a turned, squashed group, one holding a third");
            // camera-perspective: three boxes going back from a 75-degree camera into a 2:1 target
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            s.add(object: this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: -1.2, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), hex: 0xd04030));
            s.add(object: this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: 0.6, y: 0.0, z: -3.0), hex: 0x40b050));
            s.add(object: this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: 4.6, y: 0.0, z: -8.0), hex: 0x4060e0));
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 75.0, near: 0.5, far: 50.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.8, z: 2.5),
                                                      at: Vec3.of(x: 0.4, y: 0.0, z: -3.0)),
                      wide: 80, high: 40);
            this.next(to: 2);
        } else if (this.stage == 2) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "camera-perspective", what: "three boxes going back from a wide camera into a 2:1 target");
            // depth-precision: two slabs 600 m broad and 1 m deep, 5 km from a camera whose near plane is 10 cm; the green
            // one's face 5 cm nearer than the red one's, the two overlapping across the frame's middle. The nearer is
            // drawn first, so a depth too coarse to part them gives the overlap to the farther, drawn last.
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<BoxGeometry> slab = new BoxGeometry.make(width: 600.0, height: 600.0, depth: 1.0);
            Shared<MeshBasicMaterial> green = new MeshBasicMaterial.make();
            green.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0x40b050);
            Shared<Mesh> near = new Mesh.make(geometry: copy slab, material: green);
            near.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 150.0, y: 0.0, z: -5000.45);
            s.add(object: near);
            Shared<MeshBasicMaterial> red = new MeshBasicMaterial.make();
            red.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0xd04030);
            Shared<Mesh> far = new Mesh.make(geometry: copy slab, material: red);
            far.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: -150.0, y: 0.0, z: -5000.5);
            s.add(object: far);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 12.0, near: 0.1, far: 10000.0, eye: Vec3.zero(), at: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: -1.0)),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 3);
        } else if (this.stage == 3) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            // where the slabs overlap, the frame's middle third, every texel is the nearer slab's, exactly
            string why = copy this.failed;
            if (why.isEmpty()) {
                for (isize y = 20; y < 28; y = y + 1) {
                    for (isize x = 26; x < 38; x = x + 1) {
                        string apart = nearTo(got: this.texelAt(x: x, y: y), want: 0x40b050);
                        if (!apart.isEmpty() && why.isEmpty()) { why = "the texel (${x}, ${y}): " + apart; }
                    }
                }
            }
            this.found.add(name: "depth-precision: where two slabs 5 km away overlap, the one 5 cm nearer covers the other in every texel",
                           why: give why);
            this.held(test: "depth-precision", what: "two slabs 5 km away, 5 cm apart");
            // geometry-primitives: a box of 6 x 6 x 6 segments, rounded by its material, turned to show three faces
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<BoxGeometry> cut = new BoxGeometry.withSegments(width: 1.0, height: 1.0, depth: 1.0, widthSegments: 6,
                                                                   heightSegments: 6, depthSegments: 6);
            Shared<Rounded> round = new Rounded.make();
            Shared<Mesh> m = new Mesh.make(geometry: cut, material: round);
            m.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 25.0, y: 35.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: m);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: 2.6), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 4);
        } else if (this.stage == 4) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "geometry-primitives", what: "a box of 6 x 6 x 6 segments rounded by its material");
            // render-target: two boxes crossing in depth, into a 50 x 30 target
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<Mesh> one = this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: -0.3, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), hex: 0xd04030);
            one.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 0.0, y: 40.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            Shared<Mesh> two = this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: 0.3, y: 0.1, z: 0.0), hex: 0x4060e0);
            two.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 0.0, y: -40.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: one);
            s.add(object: two);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 1.2, z: 2.8), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 50, high: 30);
            this.next(to: 5);
        } else if (this.stage == 5) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "render-target", what: "two boxes crossing in depth in a 50 x 30 target");
            // nodes: a program's own node material on a turned box
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<Gradient> look = new Gradient.make();
            Shared<Mesh> m = this.boxWith(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.zero(), look: look);
            m.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 40.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: m);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.6, z: 2.6), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 6);
        } else if (this.stage == 6) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "nodes", what: "a program's own node material, a gradient in world space shaded by a direction");
            // nodes-override: the standard material's four slots set to nodes that vary over the box, under a sun and an
            // ambient light
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<MeshStandardMaterial> look = new MeshStandardMaterial.make();
            Vec3Node p = positionWorld();
            Vec3Node tint = p * 0.6 + 0.5;
            look.colorNodeMut() = Optional::Some(value: saturate(x: tint));
            FloatNode rough = p.x() + 0.5;
            look.roughnessNodeMut() = Optional::Some(value: saturate(x: rough));
            FloatNode metal = p.y() + 0.5;
            look.metalnessNodeMut() = Optional::Some(value: saturate(x: metal));
            Vec3Node glow = vec3(x: constant(value: 0.0), y: constant(value: 0.02), z: constant(value: 0.06));
            look.emissiveNodeMut() = Optional::Some(value: glow);
            Shared<Mesh> m = this.boxWith(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.zero(), look: look);
            m.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 40.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: m);
            Shared<DirectionalLight> sun = new DirectionalLight.make();
            sun.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 2.0, y: 3.0, z: 2.5);
            sun.intensityMut() = 2.0;
            s.add(object: sun);
            Shared<AmbientLight> sky = new AmbientLight.make();
            sky.intensityMut() = 0.3;
            s.add(object: sky);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.6, z: 2.6), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 7);
        } else if (this.stage == 7) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "nodes-override", what: "the standard material's colour, roughness, metalness and emissive slots set to nodes");
            // material-unlit: an unlit box beside a lit one of the same colour, under a strong sun and an ambient light
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<Mesh> flat = this.unlitBox(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: -0.7, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), hex: 0xe08030);
            flat.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 35.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: flat);
            Shared<MeshStandardMaterial> lit = new MeshStandardMaterial.make();
            lit.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0xe08030);
            Shared<Mesh> shaded = this.boxWith(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.of(x: 0.7, y: 0.0, z: 0.0), look: lit);
            shaded.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 35.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: shaded);
            Shared<DirectionalLight> sun = new DirectionalLight.make();
            sun.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 1.0, y: 3.0, z: 2.0);
            sun.intensityMut() = 3.0;
            s.add(object: sun);
            Shared<AmbientLight> sky = new AmbientLight.make();
            sky.intensityMut() = 0.4;
            s.add(object: sky);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.3, z: 3.0), at: Vec3.zero()),
                      wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 8);
        } else if (this.stage == 8) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            // the unlit box's three faces, at points well inside each, are its colour exactly, whatever the light
            string why = copy this.failed;
            if (why.isEmpty()) {
                why = nearTo(got: this.texelAt(x: 17, y: 16), want: 0xe08030);
                string side = nearTo(got: this.texelAt(x: 19, y: 26), want: 0xe08030);
                if (why.isEmpty()) { why = copy side; }
            }
            this.found.add(name: "material-unlit: an unlit box under a strong sun is its own colour on every face it shows", why: give why);
            this.held(test: "material-unlit", what: "an unlit box beside a lit one of its colour, under a strong sun");
            // light-units: a box under a 100,000-lux sun and a 20,000-lux ambient light at EV100 15, the default curve
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<MeshStandardMaterial> look = new MeshStandardMaterial.make();
            look.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0xb0a090);
            look.roughnessMut() = 0.6;
            Shared<Mesh> m = this.boxWith(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.zero(), look: look);
            m.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 35.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: m);
            Shared<DirectionalLight> sun = new DirectionalLight.make();
            sun.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 2.0, y: 3.0, z: 1.5);
            sun.intensityMut() = 100000.0;
            s.add(object: sun);
            Shared<AmbientLight> sky = new AmbientLight.make();
            sky.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0x9ab0d0);
            sky.intensityMut() = 20000.0;
            s.add(object: sky);
            Shared<PerspectiveCamera> cam = new PerspectiveCamera.make(fovRad: radians(deg: 50.0), near: 0.1, far: 100.0);
            cam.exposureMut() = ev100Sunlight();
            cam.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.6, z: 2.6);
            cam.lookAt(target: Vec3.zero());
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: cam, wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 9);
        } else if (this.stage == 9) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "light-units", what: "a box under a 100,000-lux sun and a 20,000-lux sky, seen at EV100 15");
            // exposure: three.js's default light on a box, seen 1.5 stops brighter than three.js's exposure of 1, no curve
            Shared<Scene> s = new Scene.make();
            Shared<MeshStandardMaterial> look = new MeshStandardMaterial.make();
            look.colorMut() = Color.fromHex(hex: 0x6080a0);
            Shared<Mesh> m = this.boxWith(size: 1.0, at: Vec3.zero(), look: look);
            m.rotationMut() = Euler.fromDegrees(x: 20.0, y: 35.0, z: 0.0, order: EulerOrder::XYZ);
            s.add(object: m);
            Shared<DirectionalLight> sun = new DirectionalLight.make();
            sun.positionMut() = Vec3.of(x: 2.0, y: 3.0, z: 1.5);
            s.add(object: sun);
            Shared<AmbientLight> sky = new AmbientLight.make();
            sky.intensityMut() = 0.2;
            s.add(object: sky);
            Shared<PerspectiveCamera> cam = this.plainCamera(fovDeg: 50.0, near: 0.1, far: 100.0, eye: Vec3.of(x: 0.0, y: 0.6, z: 2.6), at: Vec3.zero());
            cam.exposureMut() = ev100For(exposure: 2.828427);
            this.draw(scene: s, cam: cam, wide: 64, high: 48);
            this.next(to: 10);
        } else if (this.stage == 10) {
            if (!this.settled()) { return false; }
            this.held(test: "exposure", what: "a box under three.js's default light, seen 1.5 stops brighter");
            DeviceErrors errs = this.device.takeErrors();
            isize n = errs.reports().length();
            string firstError = n > 0 ? errs.reports()[0].message() : "";
            this.found.add(name: "the features' goldens: their frames raise no WebGPU error",
                           why: errs.isEmpty() ? "" : "the channel holds ${n} error(s), the first: " + firstError);
            this.renderer = Optional::None;
            this.stage = DONE;
        }
        return this.stage == DONE;
    }
}
